     - Verified: In [`src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c:173`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c#L173), `memset(d, 0, ...)` sets `d->current_port = 0`, which is `DEV_FBCTRL_PORT_COMMAND` (valid). Because `idata` is `uint64_t` ([`dev_fbctrl.c:110`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c#L110)), any value `>= 8` (including sign-extended negatives) triggers refusal. Valid writes only store values in `[0, 7]`.
  2. Comment 2: `"It used to be stored with only a warning, and the next DATA access then ended the emulator in the range check below. Announced once per device."`
     - Verified: On HEAD, lines 118-123 stored `d->current_port = idata` unconditionally and warned; lines 139-143 (`DEV_FBCTRL_DATA`) called `exit(1)`. `d->warned_port` is per `struct fbctrl_data` instance allocated in [`dev_fbctrl.c:172`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c#L172).
  3. Comment 3: `"unreachable while the PORT arm refuses; kept as a tripwire for a later edit that lets a bad selector in."`
     - Verified: `d->current_port` is modified nowhere else in the codebase. As long as `idata >= DEV_FBCTRL_NPORTS` guards the store, `d->current_port` remains in `[0, 7]`.

